Finger for MPW

Tested with MPW 3.5 (SC 8 and Link) on System 7.6.1.

In the MPW Shell:
    Directory "Disk:Mill Plug-In SDK:MPW:"
    Make -f Finger.make > Finger.out; Finger.out

This makes Finger, the Plug-In. Put it in Mill's "Mill Plug-Ins" folder.

What matters in Finger.make:
- SC -b puts strings in the code. A code resource has no globals.
- Link -rt MPlg=128 makes the code resource; -m MILLMAIN names the entry
  (pascal names are upper case); -sg Finger keeps it in one segment and
  names the resource.
- MillGlue.c.o is linked first, and MillMain is the first function in
  it, so the entry is at byte 0.
- -t MPlg -c MiLL set the file's type and creator.

For a Plug-In of your own, copy Finger.make and change the file names.
